  "_about": "The demo of the travel template: one space, three people, every module filled. Read by server/demo-loader.js, which writes it through the real module routes. Dates are offsets, never absolute: \"today+N\" is N days after the day the loader runs, \"start+N\" is N days after the trip start (today plus \"anchor\" days); a time follows as \"T09:30\", a trailing \"Z\" gives a full timestamp (\"start+1T19:00Z\"), and \"ms:\" in front gives a number of milliseconds (\"ms:today+2T10:00\", \"ms:now\"). \"@login\" is that person's key (in a value or a key), \"{space}\" the space id, \"{base}\" the server address. \"as\" is the person whose session writes a step (default: the first moderator); \"count\" lists the key prefixes the report counts and \"what\" names them in the sentence that says a module was skipped. A phase is named by its id in the template. Nothing here is an absolute date, so the demo stays ahead of the day on every run.",
