            "link:r2": {"text":"Board at the first stop, go before nine, and mind your pockets.","sub":"","kind":"link","title":"Riding Tram 28 without the queue","url":"https://example.com/lisbon-tram-28","excerpt":"Board at the first stop, go before nine, and mind your pockets.","tags":["lisbon"],"date":"today+5","by":"Sam Okafor","at":"today+6T10:00Z"},
            "link:r3": {"text":"Pena first, then Regaleira, with a bus between them. Skip the Moorish Castle if you are short of time.","sub":"","kind":"link","title":"Sintra in one day","url":"https://example.com/sintra-one-day","excerpt":"Pena first, then Regaleira, with a bus between them. Skip the Moorish Castle if you are short of time.","tags":["sintra"],"date":"start+3","by":"Lee Chen","at":"today+7T10:00Z"},
            "answer:r4": {"text":"For three days of trams, metro and two or three entries (Jeronimos, Belem Tower) it pays for itself. If you walk everywhere and visit one museum, buy single tickets instead.","sub":"","kind":"answer","title":"Is the Lisboa Card worth it?","content":"For three days of trams, metro and two or three entries (Jeronimos, Belem Tower) it pays for itself. If you walk everywhere and visit one museum, buy single tickets instead.","tags":["lisbon","money"],"date":"today+7","by":"Mia Alvarez","at":"today+8T10:00Z"}
